  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Trump-backed John Sununu wins New Hampshire Republican Senate primary",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/08/new-hampshire-republican-senate-primary",
      "description": "<p>Frontrunner Sununu beats Scott Brown to earn Republican nod in closely watched race in November</p><p>Former senator John E Sununu triumphed on Tuesday in the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-hampshire\">New Hampshire</a> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/republicans\">Republican</a> Senate primary Scott Brown, earning the GOP nod in what will likely be a must-win race if Democrats hope to seize the upper chamber.</p><p>Sununu, 61, was the clear frontrunner in the GOP primary. He served one term in the Senate from 2003 to 2009.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/08/new-hampshire-republican-senate-primary\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-09T00:08:22"
    },
    {
      "title": "Congressman Chris Pappas wins New Hampshire Democratic Senate primary",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/08/new-hampshire-democratic-senate-primary",
      "description": "<p>Pappas fends off challenge from progressive Karishma Manzur in seat to be vacated by retiring Jeanne Shaheen</p><p>Congressman Chris Pappas beat back progressive challenger Karishma Manzur in the Democratic primary for US Senate on Tuesday, advancing as most observers expected to what will be a closely watched general election that is critical to Democratic hopes of flipping the upper chamber.</p><p>The two were competing for the nomination that opened up after Jeanne Shaheen, 79, the state’s three‑term incumbent Democratic senator, announced her retirement.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/08/new-hampshire-democratic-senate-primary\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-09T00:04:05"
    }
  ]
